BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF WHAT'S A SNOW LEOPARD TO YOU?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T200000
UID:bm-6419220261102@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/snowleopa
 rd.png?cb=1791463924
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin Flying Books and Skyhorse for a conversati
 on between Chen-Fu Hsu\, author of\nWhat’s a Snow Leopard to You?\n*\nan
 d Lee Suksi\, author of\nThe Nerves.\n*Winner of the 2021 Taiwan Literatur
 e Award*\nWhat’s a Snow Leopard to You? i\ns a captivating blend of trav
 el writing\, fiction\, history\, and nature.\n\nFollow a young Taiwanese n
 aturalist into the breathtaking landscapes of Tibet in search of the elusi
 ve snow leopard\, while a long-lost monk’s diary offers a window onto a 
 changing Tibet and its rich cultural history.\n\nBeautifully written and r
 ichly layered\, Chen-Fu Hsu’s debut explores landscape\, memory\, wildli
 fe\, and our complicated relationship with the natural world.\nChen-Fu Hsu
  (徐振輔) is a Taiwanese writer whose work explores the entanglements b
 etween human and non-human worlds. He holds a BS in Entomology and an MA i
 n Geography from National Taiwan University. His debut novel\,\nWhat’s a
  Snow Leopard to You?\n\, has received multiple literary prizes in Taiwan.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR AN AUTHOR SOCIAL WITH EVA JURCZYK AND SAMANTHA M. BAIL
 EY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T203000
UID:bm-6528020261109@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Eva_and_S
 am___1_.png?cb=1791402059
DESCRIPTION:[Author Social]\nJoin author Eva Jurczyk in conversation with 
 Samantha M. Bailey for an Author Social!\nThe Paris Files\nis a sophistica
 ted\, character-driven thriller in which a romantic rendezvous in Paris tu
 rns disastrous after the disappearance of a new lover.\nIn the tradition o
 f\nBig Little Lies\n\, this story unfolds entirely through police intervie
 ws\, where threads of the just-out-of-reach truth tangle and snag as we he
 ar from neighbours\, friends and witnesses. Contradictory accounts\, secre
 ts and an unreliable narrator make for a deeply twisty\, up-all-night myst
 ery.\nFree to attend\, but we have limited spots -  please\nRSVP HERE\n.\
 nEva Jurczyk\nwas born in Katowice\, Poland and wound up halfway around th
 e world in a Canadian city that often masquerades as New York in the movie
 s. As her day job\, she buys books\, building library collections for the 
 University of Toronto Libraries\, and by night she writes mystery novels i
 ncluding the bestselling 6:40 to Montreal. She lives in Toronto with her h
 usband and son.\nShortlisted for Canada Reads 2025\,\nSamantha M. Bailey\n
 is an award-nominated\, USA TODAY\, and #1 international bestselling autho
 r of psychological suspense. Her work has been sold in fourteen countries\
 , translated into more than ten languages\, and optioned for screen. She l
 ives in Toronto\, where she can usually be found tapping away at her compu
 ter or curled up on her couch with a book. Samantha is currently working o
 n her next novel.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF WHOOSH
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T200000
UID:bm-6433220261112@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Whoosh.pn
 g?cb=1790278585
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin Flying Books and Goose Lane for the launch
  of\nWhoosh\nby Michael Trussler\, featuring special guests Cassidy McFadz
 ean and Daniel Scott Tysdal\, hosted by Jim Johnstone.\nPart exploration o
 f ecological collapse\, part memoir undressing a late-life Autism diagnosi
 s.\n\nMichael Trussler’s\nWhoosh\nis an unwavering collection of “ramb
 les / more rogue than feral.” Bypassing the limitations of linear though
 t\, this unforgettable book is a maelstrom of the contemporary moment that
 ’s simultaneously urgent and adrift\, floating and incisive.\n\nTrussler
  draws influence from modern artistic movements\, political insecurity\, t
 he internet\, and environmental grief to dovetail both the unexpected and 
 the intimately familiar. Lyric and experimental\, these blazing poems coll
 apse in on themselves and each other\, lines and thoughts expanding and co
 lliding to perfectly embody the connectedness of our world’s chaos.\nMic
 hael Trussler’s work engages with the beauty and violence of the twentie
 th and twenty-first centuries from a neurodivergent\, fluid perspective. H
 is writing encompasses several genres and modes of expression\, ranging fr
 om the lyrical to the avant-garde. Trussler teaches English at the Univers
 ity of Regina and is the author of seven books\, including 1\n0:10\; The H
 istory Forest\n\, winner of the Saskatchewan Book Award for Poetry\; the s
 hort fiction collection\nEncounters\,\nwinner of the Saskatchewan Book of 
 the Year Award\; and a memoir entitled\nThe Sunday Book\,\nwhich won the S
 askatchewan Book Award in both the Non-Fiction and City of Regina categori
 es. Deeply compelled by the natural world\, Trussler hikes in the Canadian
  Rockies at every opportunity.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR OUR NOVEMBER FICTION BOOK CLUB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T203000
UID:bm-6596220261116@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/NOV_2026_
 FICTION_BOOK_CLUB.jpg?cb=1792189188
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nEtna\nby Paul Yoon\, is a story told through the 
 eyes of an ex-military dog. After surviving years of a devastating war\, E
 tna decides to leave the men he has fought alongside for years and sets ou
 t on an odyssey across a war-torn country in search of home\, hope\, and a
  life beyond conflict. Along the way\, he encounters other animals and hum
 ans who are attempting to figure out how to start again. What makes a life
  when there is no home to go back to? How do we begin to trust each other 
 again after such profound loss? This is a novel about the power of an idea
 \, about never giving up\, and ultimately a novel about finding hope in th
 e most dire of times.\nJoin us on Monday\, November 16th and Tuesday\, Nov
 ember 17th for a moving conversation. We hope to see you there.\nYour book
  club ticket includes:\nA glass of wine (or another beverage of your choic
 e).\nA thoughtful conversation with our brilliant moderator\, Lee Suksi.\n
 A $20 credit toward any book in the shop.*\nGET YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nA few 
 details:\nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n*$20 book credit is valid o
 n the night of attendance only (non-refundable and non-transferable).\nWin
 e is served on the night of the event (ID required).\nTickets are non-refu
 ndable within 7 days of the event\; due to limited capacity and planning\,
  we’re not able to transfer tickets to future book club sessions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
